id: pm-2qahia
title: "GH-1135: item_hash_version 2 still masks writer hash divergence as corruption"
description: "GitHub #1135 reproduces supported pm writers computing different history hashes while stamping the same item_hash_version=2, so pinned readers classify version skew as hash/chain corruption and history-repair can truthfully report changed=false while rewriting bytes."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[6]: "area:history","area:sdk",compatibility,context-integrity,github-1135,regression
created_at: "2026-08-28T08:13:08.155Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T06:12:16.918Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#d28e5412fa32fcac38263ad0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A released-version fixture proves whether identical epoch-2 content can hash differently; every hash-input or algorithm change advances a format capability or preserves the previous comparator; drift diagnostics distinguish unsupported writer/version skew from same-version corruption; history events expose sufficient writer capability provenance for deterministic diagnosis; repair changed receipts match actual byte writes; SDK CLI health validate and repair contracts carry the distinction; focused cross-version packed-consumer and exact repository coverage gates pass
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: critical
confidence: high
severity: critical
environment: Global pm 2026.8.23 writes trackers read by repository-pinned 2026.8.20 and 2026.8.21 binaries
repro_steps: "Create and mutate an item with pm 2026.8.23, run pinned health --strict-exit, compare item_hash_version and hashes, run pinned history-repair, then compare changed receipt, bytes, and both readers' verdicts."
component: "history hashing, drift diagnostics, and repair receipts"
regression: true
customer_impact: "Ordinary cross-version mutations make CI report corruption, train operators to normalize real integrity alarms away, and hide evidence-rewriting repairs behind a false no-change receipt."
